### Create every week of 2026, open (run again: adds only missing weeks)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/production-weeks/years/2026

### List 2026's weeks (leave out year for every week)
GET http://localhost:3001/api/production-weeks?year=2026

### Wafers scheduled against each week's capacity in 2026 (active lots, by contract ship date)
GET http://localhost:3001/api/production-weeks/scheduled?year=2026

### Lots scheduled in week 7 of 2026 (active, contract ship date in the week)
GET http://localhost:3001/api/production-weeks/2026/7/lots

### Can a stored lot be scheduled into week 7 of 2026?
GET http://localhost:3001/api/production-weeks/2026/7/schedule-check?lotId=LOT-002

### Can a lot that isn't stored yet be scheduled into week 7 of 2026?
GET http://localhost:3001/api/production-weeks/2026/7/schedule-check?waferCount=25&chipType=Z_SERIES&processType=B

### Get week 7 of 2026
GET http://localhost:3001/api/production-weeks/2026/7

### Close week 7 of 2026
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/production-weeks/2026/7/status
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"closed"}

### Set week 7's capacity in wafers (null or missing type = any; [] clears it)
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/production-weeks/2026/7/capacities
Content-Type: application/json

[
  {"waferCount":1200},
  {"chipType":"Z_SERIES","waferCount":500},
  {"processType":"B","waferCount":300},
  {"chipType":"Z_SERIES","processType":"A","waferCount":100}
]

###
